<title>NETHERLANDS: Amsterdam police take Mickey Mouse approach to PR.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam police take Mickey Mouse approach to PR.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amsterdam is to send its police chief to Disneyland Paris in a bid to improve the force's relations with the public.</p>
<p>Incoming chief inspector Jelle Kuiper will visit the park to see how staff are taught the art of customer service, De Telegraaf newspaper reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;They know better than anyone else there how one can be of service to clients,&quot; Kuiper told the paper. &quot;We want to see how these workers are trained.&quot;</p>
<p>Similar training could benefit his officers, he said.</p>
<p>&quot;They don't have to be smiling all day long, that's just dumb. But we could use some work on our image, as the policeman on the beat is an important calling card for any city.&quot;</p>
</text>
